          "title": "Subjects, Not Authors: The Authorship Hazard in Agentic Dataspaces",
          "title_zh": "是主体，而非作者：智能体数据空间中的作者身份风险",
          "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2609.30614v2",
          "source": "arXiv",
          "section": "arxiv_other",
          "organization": "",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2609.30614",
          "summary": "The paper names an authorship hazard in agentic dataspaces: agents that both author and are subject to policy can write the norms that bind them, and it argues that an agent should be a subject of the governance plane, never an author of it. Across 90 preregistered edits evaluated on 344,512 requests, it finds that six edits which only reclassify a field all change authorization and narrow a duty without touching policy text, and that compiled tool-call constraints kept protected fields from reaching the model in 105 of 105 cases.",
