          "title_zh": "音频大模型知道自己听不清你说话",
          "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2609.30625v2",
          "source": "arXiv",
          "section": "arxiv_other",
          "organization": "",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2609.30625",
          "summary": "The authors study whether an audio LLM can recognize when its own transcription of degraded speech is unreliable, finding that prompting the model to judge itself works poorly, as do speech-quality predictors, generation uncertainty, and transcript-conditioned WER estimation, while reliability is strongly represented in the frozen audio encoder. A lightweight predictor trained on those encoder representations reaches 81.10% in-domain and 78.09% cross-domain macro-F1, beating the strongest baselines by 10.33 and 11.93 points, and can trigger a clarification request without modifying the underlying model.",
